-- ============================================================================
-- pin_drop_central_pa_osm.sql -- 36 new places on Pin Drop's Central PA map
-- (Nov 28 2026), with coordinates from OpenStreetMap, not memory.
--
-- Source: Randy's Overpass Turbo export, content/maps/central-pa-places.geojson
-- (OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL -- credited on /info). Of its 306 places,
-- these are the ones a room could find: public airports, colleges, the big
-- fun spots, speedways and drive-ins, the best-known museums and homes, and
-- three lookouts. Left out: private airstrips, campus buildings, offices
-- tagged as museums, hospitals and high schools (agreed Nov 28), and
-- places already on the map or next to one (ZooAmerica, the Hershey Story).
--
-- Each pin is the middle of the place's outline in OpenStreetMap; its circle
-- comes from the outline's size (at least 0.3 mi, at most 1.2). Prompts leave
-- the town off (it would turn the round into "find the town"); the reveal
-- names it. Two are CLUE rounds: Wheatland (the only president born in
-- Pennsylvania) and Julius Sturgis (America's first commercial pretzel
-- bakery, 1861).
--
-- With these, Central PA has 78 places, so it plays 12 rounds instead of 8.
-- Not in OpenStreetMap's museum list, so not here: the Eisenhower farm (add
-- it in the pin editor, or ask Claude for a second query).
--
-- Run once; fix anything after that in the pin editor (/admin/pin-drop).
-- !! Re-running it later would put these places back where they are here,
-- !! undoing the editor's fixes. Safe to run the first time and harmless to
-- !! run twice in a row: each place is added or updated by (kind, label).
-- ============================================================================

